# Vendored third-party whois responses: store and check out VERBATIM.
#
# Two reasons not to let git normalize line endings here:
#   1. ATTRIBUTION.md claims these are upstream's files at a named commit — that claim
#      only holds if the bytes are upstream's bytes.
#   2. Some of them (likexian's testdata) genuinely use CRLF, which makes them the
#      corpus's only real test of the tokenizer's \r\n normalization (plan §2). Rewriting
#      them to LF would quietly delete the thing they're useful for.
* -text
